    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Qing Mao Mountain chapters show Blood Guillotine as a rank five combat swarm without naming a cultivation path for it.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Immortal Crane Sect elders list Blood Sea’s nine true inheritances and end the list with the rank six Immortal Gu blood deity, calling Blood Sea Ancestor someone who achieved great success in blood path.",
        "chapters": [
          407
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "blood-deity-naming-later",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_blood_sea",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "char_blood_sea_ancestor",
          "path_blood"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At Lang Ya blessed land, Fang Yuan writes a remnant recipe for rank six Blood Deity; the land spirit calls it a blood path recipe and rejects the exchange because conflicts in the patched steps leave only a very small chance of successful refinement. Fang Yuan recalls that he obtained that recipe as a remnant piece, that he abandoned refining Blood Deity in his previous life mainly because the recipe was inaccurate, and that he later chose Spring Autumn Cicada instead.",
        "chapters": [
          463
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "blood-deity-naming-later",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Blood Guillotine Gu advances into rank six demonic Gu Blood Deity, which ranks seventh among the Top Ten Great Demonic Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "blood-deity-naming-later",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The later Immortal Gu and true-inheritance passages name Blood Deity without naming Blood Guillotine as its prior form.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "blood-deity-naming-later",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Each worm is about fingertip size, shaped like a locust, with a scary face, and red all over. The group flies as a red cloud or a red tornado.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Blood Guillotine is a rank five Gu. Each worm is about fingertip size, locust-shaped, red all over, with a scary face, and the group flies as a red cloud or tornado.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Its strength scales hard with numbers. At peak it can engulf skies and lands and outmatch many rank six Gu; at one or two individuals it is worse than a rank three Gu. Without a user it can only attack head on, which leaves it weak against wide area countermeasures such as the thunder crown wolf’s rank four Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Usability and feeding are fused into one. The swarm enters living bodies, drains blood, and in a few breaths multiplies from one into many. Beast blood can be sucked dry for killing, but only a Gu Master’s origin blood that contains primeval essence lets the Gu multiply. When hungry and starved of that food, the worms eat each other and shrink the group to keep moving.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Blood Guillotine Gu advances into the rank six demonic Gu Blood Deity, that Blood Deity ranks 7th among the Top Ten Great Demonic Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_blood_deity",
          "sys_top_ten_great_demonic_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Much later, Fang Yuan still treats rank five blood guillotine Gu as the familiar example of a Gu that combines use and nurturing, and as a type with a vile reputation.",
        "chapters": [
          663
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "First gen Gu Yue brings rank five Blood Guillotine out of the blood lake against Tie Xue Leng’s giant puppet, together with a pack of almost a thousand bladewing blood bats. First gen Gu Yue has operated at that place for almost a thousand years. Heaven Earth Magnificent Sound Gu, used at full power through the puppet, kills numerous Blood Guillotine across the sky as well as the nearby bats.",
        "chapters": [
          186
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-gen-gu-yues-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_first_gen_gu_yue",
          "char_tie_xue_leng",
          "gu_heaven_earth_magnificent_sound_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lord Sky Crane later rages that both the blood guillotine and the bladewing blood bat Gu were supposed to be his. As Immortal Crane Sect brothers they found a Blood Sea Ancestor true treasure inheritance; Lord Sky Crane obtained it, then First gen Gu Yue stole the Gu and fled. First gen Gu Yue orders blood guillotine and bladewing blood bat Gu to cut Raise Eyebrows and Exhale Gu’s white eyebrows, then turns them on Lord Sky Crane when cutting fails.",
        "chapters": [
          192
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-gen-gu-yues-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lord_sky_crane",
          "gu_bladewing_blood_bat_gu",
          "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
          "gu_raise_eyebrows_and_exhale_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He later sends them to defend the village,",
        "chapters": [
          193
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-gen-gu-yues-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "and still later against Bai Ning Bing’s glacier, where large numbers of them crash into the ice to slow it.",
        "chapters": [
          195
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-gen-gu-yues-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bai_ning_bing"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": true,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Feeding is the same act as combat use: Gu Master lives, bodies, and life-bound origin blood with primeval essence. Clan memorials say the first generation ancestor left these Gu and that they require Gu Masters’ lives before they will defend the clan.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "feeding",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
