  "distribution": {
    "locations": [
      "reg_southern_border"
    ],
    "factions": [],
    "origin": "unknown",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "During the thunder crown wolf crisis, Gu Masters sit on the village square and willingly let the swarm feed, leaving white bones once the Gu are satisfied and swell to tens of thousands. The swarm then tears through ordinary lightning wolves, struggles against the thunder crown wolf’s lightning, drills under its armor to suck blood, and finally thins out and flies a circuit around the village before vanishing into the clouds. The last prior crisis that used this defense was about two hundred years earlier; the first generation clan head had been dead for at least a thousand years.",
        "chapters": [
          165
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "clan-defense-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The summoning ritual sits only in the clan’s secret records, not in the falsified official history shown to outsiders.",
        "chapters": [
          180
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "clan-defense-on-qing-mao-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Blood guillotine was the Blood Sea Ancestor’s last fusion accomplishment after bladewing blood bat and blood frenzy Gu. Usability and feeding are fused; it sustains itself through wars, multiplies by swallowing Gu Masters’ blood, and does not need a Gu Master to supply primeval essence. He was a rank seven demonic path Gu Master researching Gu that could still absorb natural primeval essence after refinement; the blood guillotine recipe was the most advanced of the three he finished before righteous path traps defeated him. After fatal wounds he seeded hundreds of thousands of inheritance grounds from the Middle Continent to the Southern Border and elsewhere, and blood guillotine is among the Gu that are easy to raise and multiply from those leftovers. Blood guillotine sits with bladewing blood bat and blood frenzy Gu among his fusion recipes; his dying line is that the blood path is not alone and that the legacy will continue for all eternity.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "origin-under-blood-sea-ancestor",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_blood_frenzy_gu",
          "reg_southern_border"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
